cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "right-size-the-model: a measurement kit for bounded language workloads"
message: >-
  If you publish numbers produced with these fixtures, please cite the
  repository and state the fixture version you used.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Alger
    given-names: Ken W.
repository-code: "https://github.com/kenwalger/right-size-the-model"
abstract: >-
  Fixtures, a runner and a scorer for measuring how much intelligence a
  bounded language workload actually requires: a deterministic baseline,
  closed-set classification, and grounded question answering including
  questions the corpus does not answer.
keywords:
  - small language models
  - local inference
  - evaluation
  - raspberry pi
  - abstention
license: MIT
